From 89ed1ec368fed09455c4dda6036e479c5de1711a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 04:44:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [v2 only] net: train raw zstd dictionary on native p2p-v2
 traffic

Capture real isolated V7/BIP340 transaction admission, 134-byte headers, block serving, compact blocks and addr traffic. Train on three disjoint signing-key/header groups and hold the fourth out. Keep immutable V1 bytes and its explicit legacy codec tests.

The 8076-byte raw-content V2 dictionary reduces held-out warm mixed bytes from 18839 to 18752 (0.46%), and cold first-message bytes from 50489 to 48052 (4.83%). Independent Python and actual C++ sessions reproduce the same warm counts. CPU is approximately unchanged for the warm mixed workload on the loaded Apple M5 Max; this is not a network throughput claim.

Include the captured corpus, deterministic trainer, interleaved comparison and framework decoder/reproduction tests. Four Python tests and C++ corpus roundtrips pass. Isolated full daemon/unit build and live modified-codec gates remain in progress; their receipts are delivered separately. Mainnet-shaped replay, other platforms and sanitizers were not run.

